# ============================================================================
# Network Module - Variables
# ============================================================================
#
# PURPOSE:
#   This file defines input variables for the Network module.
#   These are the parameters that must be provided when calling this module.
#   The module abstracts provider-specific networking concepts behind a common
#   set of variables.
#
# KEY CONCEPTS FOR BEGINNERS:
#   - Module variables: Inputs that the calling module must provide
#   - Required vs optional: Variables without defaults are required
#   - Variable types: Same as root module variables (string, number, bool, etc.)
#   - Module inputs: Passed from root module using module block
#   - Provider abstraction: Variables use generic names (VPC CIDR) that work across providers
#
# TERRAFORM DOCUMENTATION:
#   - Module Variables: https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/modules/develop/variables
#   - Module Inputs: https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/language/modules/syntax#calling-a-child-module
#
# USAGE EXAMPLE:
#   In the root module, you would call this module like:
#   module "network" {
#     source = "./modules/network"
#     vpc_cidr = "10.0.0.0/16"
#     # ... other variables
#   }
# ============================================================================

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED VARIABLES
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# CIDR block for the VPC/VNet
# This defines the IP address range for your network
# Format: CIDR notation (e.g., "10.0.0.0/16")
# Examples:
#   - "10.0.0.0/16" = 65,536 IPs (AWS VPC, Azure VNet)
#   - "10.0.0.0/24" = 256 IPs (smaller network)
# Note: Terminology varies by provider:
#   - AWS: VPC CIDR
#   - Azure: VNet address space
#   - GCP: VPC network CIDR
variable "vpc_cidr" {
  description = "CIDR block for the VPC/VNet (IP address range for the network)"
  type        = string
  # No default - this must be provided by the calling module
}

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE: Additional Variables
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# In a complete module implementation, you would also have variables for:
# - project_prefix: Prefix for resource names
# - region: Cloud provider region
# - availability_zones: List of AZs for subnet deployment
# - subnet_cidrs: List of subnet CIDR blocks
# - enable_nat_gateway: Whether to create NAT gateway
# - enable_flow_logs: Whether to enable network flow logging
# - tags: Resource tags
# - existing_vpc_id: Optional existing VPC to use instead of creating new one
# - And other provider-specific configuration options
